WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.955 --> 00:00:10.005
HQ, the deal desk. Payments, trades, the F and I menu, credit, contracts and e-sign, on one screen.

2
00:00:10.906 --> 00:00:20.702
Marcus is buying a Road Glide with a trade. The strip on top is the deal at a glance: payment, amount financed, front gross, back gross and where it stands.

3
00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:31.678
The payment grid. Columns own the term, rows own the cash down. Click any cell and it becomes the live deal, the one every form prints from.

4
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:42.321
The worksheet underneath is plain: price, trade, payoff, cash down, tax, fees. Change the rate or the lender and everything above it recomputes.

5
00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:53.558
The F and I menu quotes each product with its effect on the payment. GAP is always quoted at the deal's term. It never prints on the buyer's order, only on the contract.

6
00:00:54.458 --> 00:01:04.018
Credit runs from the deal. Push to the bureau, push to the lenders, rate products live. The decision comes back to this screen with the buy rate, max term and reserve.

7
00:01:04.921 --> 00:01:13.867
Print and send. Six documents go out for e-signature by text and email. Each one shows its status until the last signature lands.

8
00:01:14.769 --> 00:01:24.404
The customer signs from a phone. A delivery card appears on the transport board on its own, and marking it delivered posts the deal to accounting and turns the buyer into an owner.

9
00:01:25.308 --> 00:01:33.289
Front and back gross visible the whole way. No re-keying between the desk, the lender and the office. That is desking in HQ.
